id: pm-3gh457
title: "Sentry PM-CLI-2V: pm init surfaces raw EACCES when the managed workspace .gitignore cannot be written"
description: "Release 2026.8.4 recorded one handled high-priority Sentry event when pm init reached ensurePmGitignore and writeFile failed with EACCES. The public SDK/CLI init boundary must return a stable actionable permission error, preserve existing workspace bytes, and classify the expected environment constraint without an unstructured high-severity exception."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T15:09:53.826Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T15:24:44.212Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-04T15:24:27.671Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-04T15:24:27.671Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A real permission-constrained .gitignore write produces a stable structured pm error rather than raw EACCES; Existing .gitignore bytes are preserved on failure; SDK and CLI callers receive actionable remediation without leaking the scrubbed path; Regression coverage exercises the real filesystem boundary and keeps successful/idempotent behavior unchanged; Full coverage, static quality, packed consumer, telemetry, and Sentry release gates pass; The Sentry issue is resolved only after exact-head verification"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: pm-cli@2026.8.4 on a permission-constrained Arch Linux workspace
repro_steps: Run pm init against a valid workspace whose .gitignore path cannot be opened for writing.
resolution: "Managed .gitignore reads and writes now convert EACCES, EPERM, and EROFS into the public init_gitignore_unwritable PmCliError with path-safe recovery; telemetry classifies it as runtime and the Sentry gate ignores only the handled structured form."
expected_result: "Permission-constrained init returns stable actionable SDK/CLI recovery, preserves unrelated .gitignore bytes, and cannot hide raw or unhandled filesystem defects."
actual_result: "Real chmod EACCES and packed npx/bunx acceptance return init_gitignore_unwritable without private path disclosure, preserve sentinel bytes, and pass exact 100% repository coverage and static contracts."
