comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T15:09:53.826Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched all statuses for PM-CLI-2V, EACCES permission denied open, gitignore permission, read-only init workspace, and neighboring Sentry/merge-install failures. pm-hous owns successful managed .gitignore creation and pm-bnmlsc owns .git/config permission classification; neither owns failure to write the managed .gitignore. Live Sentry evidence: PM-CLI-2V id 138799498, unresolved/high, handled, count 1, release pm-cli@2026.8.4, first/last seen 2026-08-04T13:15:45.639Z, stack ensurePmGitignore -> node writeFile."
  "2026-08-04T15:16:53.860Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the new real permission-constrained .gitignore test failed first because ensurePmGitignore propagated raw EACCES; after implementation the 3-file focused suite passes 63/63, targeted ESLint and typecheck pass, generated error catalog/contracts are current, and the SDK surface records one intentional additive error code."
  "2026-08-04T15:24:16.692Z","harness:codex","Exact-head evidence: quality:static passes including tracker ratchets and SDK import/CLI transport floors; contracts and generated error catalog are current; full coverage passes 432 files / 6838 tests at 100% statements (48651/48651), branches (35245/35245), functions (9958/9958), and lines (47154/47154). The linked 3-file acceptance suite passes 63/63. A fresh packed consumer proves both npx and bunx return exit 1 with code init_gitignore_unwritable, omit the private /tmp path from detail, and preserve sentinel .gitignore bytes. Sentry PM-CLI-2V will be resolved against the resulting exact commit, then the live gate will be rerun."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T15:24:17.180Z","harness:codex","Expected filesystem constraints need a stable public SDK error at the narrow I/O boundary, path-safe recovery context, and an observability allowlist keyed to the structured PmCliError message and handled state; raw Error and unhandled variants must remain release-blocking."
